{"name":"Mantis","hex":"#74c365","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mantis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Mantidae – type genus of the order Mantodea of mantises."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mantis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mantis","blocks":[{"text":"Mantises are an order (Mantodea) of insects that contains over 2,400 species in about 460 genera in 33 families. The largest family is the Mantidae (\"mantids\"). Mantises are distributed worldwide in temperate and tropical habitats. They have triangular heads with bulging eyes supported on flexible necks. Their elongated bodies may or may not have wings, but all mantodeans have forelegs that are greatly enlarged and adapted for catching and gripping prey; their upright posture, while remaining stationary with forearms folded, resembling a praying posture, has led to the common name praying mantis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Mantis_%28European%29.jpg/330px-Mantis_%28European%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantis","wikidata":"Q131250"},{"title":"Mantis (Marvel Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Mantis is a character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by writer Steve Englehart and artist Don Heck, the character first appeared in The Avengers #112. Mantis has been depicted as a member of the Avengers and the Guardians of the Galaxy, as well as the mother of Sequoia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8c/Mantismadona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantis_(Marvel_Comics)","wikidata":"Q2009899"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are 